msgstr "Target URL"

msgid "The \"Use OAuth\" option has been disabled: this webhook is authenticated with a token of the Bearer API plugin. To use the native OAuth 2.0 authentication of GLPI, select \"Native GLPI (OAuth 2.0)\" as API authentication source."
msgstr "The \"Use OAuth\" option has been disabled: this webhook is authenticated with a token of the Bearer API plugin. To use the native OAuth 2.0 authentication of GLPI, select \"Native GLPI (OAuth 2.0)\" as API authentication source."

msgid "The additional parameters must be a valid JSON object."
msgstr "The additional parameters must be a valid JSON object."

msgid "The bearer token has been refreshed."
msgstr "The bearer token has been refreshed."

msgid "The challenge-response authentication is enabled for this webhook (\"Security\" tab or GLPI_WEBHOOK_CRA_MANDATORY constant): GLPI sends its verification request without the bearer token, so a protected API (such as the API of another GLPI) refuses it and the webhook is never sent."
msgstr "The challenge-response authentication is enabled for this webhook (\"Security\" tab or GLPI_WEBHOOK_CRA_MANDATORY constant): GLPI sends its verification request without the bearer token, so a protected API (such as the API of another GLPI) refuses it and the webhook is never sent."

msgid "The token URL is not configured."
msgstr "The token URL is not configured."

msgid "The token is renewed this much time before its expiration."
msgstr "The token is renewed this much time before its expiration."

msgid "The token is requested from the token URL of the provider, then added to the requests sent to the target URL of the webhook. The requests actually sent (URL, status code) are listed in the \"Queries log\" tab."
msgstr "The token is requested from the token URL of the provider, then added to the requests sent to the target URL of the webhook. The requests actually sent (URL, status code) are listed in the \"Queries log\" tab."

msgid "The token response is not a valid JSON object."
msgstr "The token response is not a valid JSON object."

#, php-format
msgid "The token settings have changed, but no new token could be obtained: %s"
msgstr "The token settings have changed, but no new token could be obtained: %s"

msgid "The token settings have changed: a new token has been obtained."
msgstr "The token settings have changed: a new token has been obtained."

msgid "The username and password are required for the \"Password\" grant type."
msgstr "The username and password are required for the \"Password\" grant type."

msgid "The webhook authenticates with the OAuth 2.0 parameters defined in the \"Security\" tab. This plugin does not add any token."
msgstr "The webhook authenticates with the OAuth 2.0 parameters defined in the \"Security\" tab. This plugin does not add any token."

msgid "The webhook is authenticated with a token delivered by the selected provider (Setup > General > Bearer APIs). The \"Use OAuth\" option of the \"Security\" tab is then disabled."
msgstr "The webhook is authenticated with a token delivered by the selected provider (Setup > General > Bearer APIs). The \"Use OAuth\" option of the \"Security\" tab is then disabled."

#, php-format
msgid "These webhooks no longer use a token provider and are back to the native authentication of GLPI: %s"
msgstr "These webhooks no longer use a token provider and are back to the native authentication of GLPI: %s"

msgid "This token URL is the one of a GLPI: GLPI only links its tokens to a user with the \"Password\" grant type. With \"Client credentials\", its API answers \"You are not authenticated\"."
msgstr "This token URL is the one of a GLPI: GLPI only links its tokens to a user with the \"Password\" grant type. With \"Client credentials\", its API answers \"You are not authenticated\"."

msgid "This token URL is the one of a GLPI: the \"api\" scope is required to use its API (otherwise it answers \"You do not have the required scope(s)\"). The OAuth client of the target GLPI must also allow this scope."
msgstr "This token URL is the one of a GLPI: the \"api\" scope is required to use its API (otherwise it answers \"You do not have the required scope(s)\"). The OAuth client of the target GLPI must also allow this scope."

msgid "This token provider is inactive or in the trash: no token is added to the requests of the webhook."
msgstr "This token provider is inactive or in the trash: no token is added to the requests of the webhook."

msgid "This token provider is inactive or in the trash: no token is added to the requests of these webhooks."
msgstr "This token provider is inactive or in the trash: no token is added to the requests of these webhooks."

msgid "This webhook does not use a token provider: choose one in the \"API authentication source\" field of the webhook form."
msgstr "This webhook does not use a token provider: choose one in the \"API authentication source\" field of the webhook form."

